## Python Statistical Analysis

## Overview

This folder contains the Python analysis performed to investigate employee attrition patterns in the IBM HR Analytics 
dataset.

Python was used to conduct statistical tests and examine relationships between selected employee characteristics and 
attrition.

## Tools and Libraries
Python
Jupyter Notebook
Pandas
SciPy
Matplotlib, if used for visualisation

## Statistical Analysis
1. Chi-Square Test of Independence

A chi-square test was used to examine the association between overtime status and employee attrition.

The objective was to assess whether overtime status and attrition were statistically associated in the dataset.

2. Independent Samples t-Test

An independent samples t-test was used to compare monthly income between employees who left the organisation and employees
who stayed.

The objective was to assess whether the observed difference in average monthly income between the two groups was s
tatistically significant.

## Analytical Approach

The analysis involved preparing the relevant variables, defining comparison groups, conducting statistical tests, and 
interpreting the results in the context of the business problem.

## Files

This folder contains the Python notebooks and supporting files used for the statistical analysis.

## Interpretation and Limitations

Statistical association does not establish causation. The results should be interpreted alongside the dataset's 
limitations and the broader organisational context.

A statistically significant result does not automatically imply that an observed difference is practically important.

## Key Takeaway

Python statistical testing adds analytical depth to the project by evaluating whether observed differences and 
associations warrant further investigation.
